# React and Next.js

- Follow the UI libraries already installed. Do not treat a React project as Next.js unless Next.js is a dependency.
- When the project uses the Next.js App Router, keep secrets and server-only access in Server Components or server functions. Add `"use client"` only for interactivity, browser APIs, or client hooks.
- Use semantic elements, accessible names, labels, keyboard access, and visible focus for interactive UI.
- Keep state as local as it is, using the state approach the project already has.
- Follow the Rules of Hooks. Do not call hooks conditionally.
- Do not duplicate a fetch on server and client, or pull a large client dependency, without a concrete need.
- Show loading, empty, and error states for async UI.
